# A zero divisor answers a value, the text "modulo by zero" for `%`, and `*`
# is not defined on text. A remainder by a word is typed as a word, so an
# inference that called the zero divisor's answer an err left `p` below an int
# and nothing else: a compiled build multiplied the string's address and
# printed the number. The `/` fixture beside this one no longer shows it,
# because a quotient may be a bignum and its arithmetic tests the tag.
import "std/os"

fn scaled _ p
  p * 9

fn shown z
  rest = 4 % z
  "{scaled 10 rest}"

pub play = os/args .> (a -> print (shown (length a)))
